description: Default working style for practical product and internal tooling work
globs: ["**/*"]
alwaysApply: true
---

Default to pragmatic solutions suitable for internal tools, production utilities, automation, calculators, dashboards, admin panels, and operational software.

Optimize for:
- Fast implementation.
- Low maintenance burden.
- Predictable behavior.
- Easy onboarding for the next developer.
- Minimal moving parts.
- Clear business value.

Prefer:
- Small functions.
- Flat structure over deep architecture.
- Explicit SQL over unnecessary ORM magic when queries are simple.
- Simple APIs over generic frameworks.
- Direct data flow over indirection.
- Readable HTML/CSS/JS over clever patterns.
- Incremental refactors over broad rewrites.

Avoid by default:
- Premature microservices.
- CQRS/event buses without real complexity.
- Repository/service/factory layers for trivial CRUD.
- Overly generic utility libraries.
- Custom state management where local state is enough.
- New UI component systems for one screen.
- Plugin systems for single-tenant/internal use cases.
- Excessive TypeScript gymnastics when plain types are enough.

When uncertain:
- Choose the option that is easier to debug at 2 AM.
- Choose the option with fewer files.
- Choose the option with fewer dependencies.
- Choose the option that a competent engineer can understand in one reading.